{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And behold, Egypt journeyed after them.</b> The verse calls them in the singular, as in 'and he came to Hebron,' and likewise 'and the ambusher arose quickly from his place.' And they were five thousand." "<b>And they were very afraid.</b> What did Israel see to be so afraid of six hundred chariots — were they not sixty myriad, all of them twenty years old and upward and armed for battle, as it is written 'and armed the children of Israel went up'? Rather, they were afraid to do battle with their masters — like a slave who is always afraid of his master."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The singular references allude to standard midrashic-style prooftexts; 'and he came to Hebron' cites Numbers 13:22 (the spies spoken of in singular), 'and the ambusher arose' is less readily identified."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:49.236484510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}